  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-cool-terminal",
      "text": "English · [中文](./README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Description",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness terminal plugin — a real shell, workspace sync, persistent state, common-command management, and command completion."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Grouped by workspace** — Consoles are grouped by your DSH Workspaces automatically, staying tidy no matter how many you open.\n- **Persistent across sessions and reloads** — Shell sessions, scrollback, and the current path are preserved across conversation switches and page reloads, picking up right where you left off.\n- **Per-console command history** — Each console keeps its own history; pressing `↑` never pulls in commands from other consoles.\n- **Common command management** — Add, edit, delete, and use the common commands you create.\n- **Inline command completion** — Typing in a console pops matching common commands up under the caret; hovering a row or pressing `↑`/`↓` selects one, and `Enter` fills it into the command line without running it.\n- **Bilingual (English / Chinese)** — Every string the plugin renders follows DSH's language setting and switches live, with new console names minted in the language on screen."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "Use DSH's add-plugin feature and enter the package name: `dsh-cool-terminal`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Current limitations",
      "text": "- Consoles run a real local shell as the DSH process user — this is not the confined one-shot shell, so treat them as a localhost-trusted environment.\n- Consoles are process-local and do not survive a DSH restart.\n- A console's size is fixed at creation; resizing is not supported yet."
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing",
      "text": "Contributions via Issues and PRs are welcome.\n\n```\n// Clone project\ngit clone https://github.com/CoolTea001/dsh-cool-terminal.git\n\n// Install dependencies"
    },
    {
